We need to parse input: {"items": ["apple", "banana", "cherry"]}
We need to transform to: {"items": [{"name": "<item>", "length": <char_count>}], "count": <total>}

Interpretation: For each item in the input array, we need to create an object with name: the item string, length: its character count. Then items array should contain these objects. Also count: total number of items (i.e., length of original items array). So output JSON.

Input items: ["apple", "banana", "cherry"]
Compute lengths:
apple -> 5
banana -> 6
cherry -> 6

So items array: [
 {"name": "apple", "length": 5},
 {"name": "banana", "length": 6},
 {"name": "cherry", "length": 6}
]

Count: 3

Thus output: {"items": [{"name": "apple", "length": 5}, {"name": "banana", "length": 6}, {"name": "cherry", "length": 6}], "count": 3}

